neighbors.abstract:
Internet routing is probably the largest scale distributed calculation&#13;
made on our planet. Its computation is based on routing protocols&#13;
whose dynamics has been observed to be highly complex, and not well understood&#13;
[1]. However, before trying to design new routing protocols we&#13;
should understand and debug the existing ones.&#13;
As a step towards improving the robustness of our routing system, we&#13;
propose to first obtain an accurate picture of interdomain routing behavior.&#13;
To achieve that we focus on developing an open source “BGP monitor and&#13;
alarm system”. In this position paper we argue that researchers and operators&#13;
should work together on a joint set of tools that are capable of monitor&#13;
the routing plane constantly.
